\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {I}{\ignorespaces Summary of Held's GHP quantities in our conventions, taken from\nobreakspace  {}\cite  {HT2}. On a mode with dependence $e^{-i\omega t + im\varphi } = e^{-i\omega u + im\varphi _*}$, one puts $\partial _u \to -i\omega $ and $\partial _{\varphi _*} \to im$. $\tilde  \hbox {\ec \char '360}$ and $\tilde  \hbox {\ec \char '360}'$ are thereby equal to the spin-raising and spin-lowering operators when acting on spin-weighted spherical harmonics; see, e.g.,\nobreakspace  {}\cite  {Chandrasekhar:1984siy}.\relax }}{4}{table.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
